  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The book contains a series of reflections about the narcissism of a painter and the emblem that he chooses to represent himself. Through Ral Veroni's texts we can trace the origin of subsequent works, with their symbols inserted in the cityscape in similar way[s] that [were] used in his last series of paintings, graffitis, and lambda prints. The book narrates the 'encounter' with a street graffiti: a heart with crossed bones. The text describes the identification with the symbol, the making of a kite following the symbol's shape, its inaugural flight in the city, and the start of a series of paintings about this subject."-- Vamp and Tramp website, accessed 4/24/2012.</subfield>
  </datafield>
